# Canonical contributor identities.
#
# git shortlog, git log and GitHub's contributor statistics read this file and
# collapse the identities on the right onto the one on the left. It changes how
# history is DISPLAYED and rewrites nothing, so hashes and signatures are
# untouched.
#
# Five author identities appear in this repository's history, all of them the
# same person: two spellings of the name, and three GitHub noreply addresses
# left by commits made through the web interface.
#
# The canonical form matches `user.name` and `user.email` in git config, so
# commits made from now on need no entry here. The published citation record
# uses the fuller "Ellyess F. Benmoufok" with an ORCID, and lives in
# CITATION.cff and .zenodo.json; that is the record for citation, and this file
# is only for reading history.
#
# Deliberately NOT mapped: the committer "GitHub <noreply@github.com>" on
# web-interface commits. GitHub genuinely was the committer there, with the
# author being the person who made the change, so the pairing is a true record
# of how those commits were created rather than a misattribution to correct.

Ellyess Benmoufok <benmoufok.ellyess@gmail.com> Ellyess F. Benmoufok <benmoufok.ellyess@gmail.com>
Ellyess Benmoufok <benmoufok.ellyess@gmail.com> Ellyess Benmoufok <39857651+EllyessB@users.noreply.github.com>
